Z||000005||Old Lar||10-15-2000||08:52 PM||||Phil:  There's nothing worse for me to drive the Fiero in the snow.  They use a lot of salt on the winter roads here and although the body panels don't rust, the space age frame etc. will.  So Fieros go into hibernation. <P>The NEFA cruise looks like fun.  I used to spend time in the Boothbay Harbor area.  Maine is a real pretty part of the country along the coast.  An 11 hour drive down east was a little too much for me this weekend.||||reg||1
