Z||000009||Old Lar||10-17-2000||12:55 PM||||Yeah, mine will go into hibernation next week.  I have to pull the seats out to repair the seat belt holder and maybe replace the seatcover on the drivers side.  It's starting to go.<P>A 3800 s/c Fiero would be a nice car..ask Phil.  For $8-12000 you could find one already together.  ACE, Ed Parks, Bob Steger and a bunch of guys in California may do these swaps routinely and know what they are doing. No one in the Rochester area that I know of does this work.<P>My daily driver is a 99 Buick GS with a 3800 s/c.<P>||||reg||1
